 8978+84A1              ;89) get_item_name	;get file name under cursor
 8979+84A1              ;IN: current active callers use SCF. 128K parser always returns full info.
 8980+84A1              ;OUT=HL=name start, BC= name length, DE= file length
 8981+84A1              ;OUT=A=0= item is a directory+ HL, BC
 8982+84A1              ;OUT=A=1=item is a file+ HL, BC
 8983+84A1              ;OUT=A=2=item type cannot be determined (because of NLST command)+ HL, BC
 8984+84A1              ;OUT=A=3= item not parsed (for the moment) bacause it is LIST in full, HL, BC irrelevant
 8985+84A1              ;OUT=A=4= starting item ".."
 8986+84A1              ;bits 1 (items 0=abbreviated, 1= full) and 3 (current command type 0=LIST, 1=NLST) from flag_dir are of interest here
 8987+84A1              ; --- DOKUMENTACE CZ: get_item_name ---
 8988+84A1              ; Ucel: Rozebere aktuální položku adresáře a vrátí jméno a typ.
